<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h1 class="display-4 fw-bold mb-3">Regulatory & Compliance Reporting</h1>
        <p class="lead mb-4">
            Maintain organizational good standing through automated statutory reporting engines 
            specifically engineered for the Zimbabwean IPEC and ZIMRA regulatory frameworks.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">IPEC Statutory Returns & Solvency</h2>
        <p>
            Eliminate the manual stress of quarterly reporting. The Regulatory module 
            automatically aggregates data from across the policy, claims, and financial 
            cores to populate IPEC-required returns. Real-time Solvency Margin calculations 
            ensure that management is always aware of the organization's regulatory 
            capital position, providing early warning signals before compliance thresholds 
            are breached.
        </p>
        <p>
            Automated generation of Premium Registers and Claims Registers—with full support for 
            multi-currency segregation—ensures that regulatory data requests can be 
            satisfied in minutes rather than days.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Tax Compliance & Withholding</h2>
        <p>
            The system manages the complex intersection of insurance and taxation. Automated 
            calculation and reporting of ZIMRA Withholding Tax on premiums (where 
            applicable) ensures that all fiscal obligations are tracked as they occur. 
            Integration with the ZIMRA fiscalization platform ensures that every 
            premium receipt is correctly registered and tagged with the required 
            regulatory signatures.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="row mb-5">
    <div class="col-lg-12">
        <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mb-4">Immutable Audit & Event Logging</h2>
        <p>
            Maintain an absolute, forensic record of organizational activity. Every structural 
            event—policy inception, claim reserve revision, underwriting referral, and 
            payment authorization—is captured in an immutable audit trail, including 
            user ID, timestamp, and "before/after" values. This granular accountability 
            is essential for satisfying IFRS 17 (Insurance Contracts) standards and 
            providing internal and external auditors with absolute confidence in 
            the system's integrity.
        </p>
        <p>
            Role-based access control (RBAC) ensures that users only have access to the 
            functions and data appropriate to their authorized department and seniority, 
            providing a foundation for organizational governance.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

